# Build-time values, baked into the binary. Copy to .env.local, which is gitignored.
#
# server/server/build.rs loads this file and re-emits each value as cargo:rustc-env, so
# `option_env!` can read it. Nothing here is read at runtime: changing a value means
# rebuilding, and a shipped binary cannot be redirected by setting the same variable in
# its environment.
#
# Precedence is real-environment, then server/.env.local, then this one at the root:
# dotenvy does not overwrite a variable that is already set. CI sets the environment and
# neither file exists there.
#
# Editing this file triggers a rebuild — build.rs declares rerun-if-changed on it.

# The BVC registry this build enrolls with and asks for its own address.
#
# Deliberately not a config key and not a runtime variable: an operator never chooses
# it, and a runtime override would be a way to aim somebody else's server at a registry
# they did not pick. A build without it refuses enrollment by name at startup.
#
# `mise run relay` prints this value at every start, as "relay registry enrollment link".
BVC_REGISTRY_PEERLINK=

# Product telemetry. Absent disables it.
POSTHOG_KEY=
POSTHOG_HOST=
